After several weeks, the landlord came to Clark's apartment to evict him.
He didn't answer the door.
No one lived there.
The landlord called the police and they opened the door.
What they found was...
...disturbing.
They found out Clark's body in bed.
He looked extremely weak.
He was hugged to what it used to be his GameStation 69
"What a loser", the landlord said.
Before leaving the apartment, the landlord saw something written on the wall using what appeared to be blood. It said\:
"I NEEDED MORE"
javi: Whoa, that was a bit strong.
javi: Hello there! My name's Javi. The developer of what you just experienced.
javi: Well, sorry if I traumatized you too much.
javi: Writing has always been a great passion for me and so is gaming so I thought of combining both in this game.
javi: Just to clarify, no dog or granny was harmed during the development of this game.
javi: Just as a reminder, the game is open source and licensed under the GPL 3
javi: You can check itch io page of the game, or its source code below
label link_options
- Check itch page
	do Global.open_url("https://google.com")
	jump link_options
- Check source code
	do Global.open_url("https://github.com/javiermoralesdev/INeedMore")
	jump link_options
- Return to main menu
	javi: Once again, thank you por playing my game.
	do Global.change_scene("main_menu")